  },
  "summary": "Block-structured LDL^T factorization of a symmetric indefinite constraint-system matrix for the vehicle dynamics solver, followed by forward/back substitution. Each of ~32 pivot blocks computes the reciprocal of a diagonal pivot, scales the corresponding L column through a column-pointer table into global workspace arrays, stores D-factor entries, and applies rank-1 outer-product updates to the remaining submatrix. The final phase accumulates dot products of factor arrays into the dbl_8D3870..dbl_8D3978 series and subtracts scaled factor products to complete the solve. Pure numerical computation: no parameters, no callees, no branches other than loop counters.",
